      {
        "id": 239538,
        "name": "der andere Jan",
        "username": "der_andere_Jan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/der_andere_jan/{size}/1881_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-07-23T17:44:36.604Z",
        "cooked": "<p>the most simple pattern I’ve been using is, the fugitive(s) create traffic-related challenges via overcome, which represent another obstacle they passed (call them ‘the railroad crossing’, the drawbridge right as it gets pulled up’ etc).<br>\nTo close in, the follower(s) have to overcome said challenges (representing driving stunts etc.)<br>\nDon’t bother too much with who’s actually doing the driving - consider both parties as one unit each, wherein anyone can overcome, and the others can boost, attack, hinder etc.</p>\n<p>Balance by giving Npc specific boosts, or add extra minions accompanying them, and how much of a headstart you give them.</p>\n<p>Whenever there are (X) or more traffic challenges unresolved, the fugitives have escaped.</p>\n<p>Nice side-effect is that together with Gyro, this results in a double-timer that makes everybody keep their focus, while there is a lot of room for creative driving shenanigans.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-07-23T17:45:29.226Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": 2,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
